  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Fisher Sand and Gravel has $13.4B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. The company holds 15 awards with an average award size of $890M, and obligations are up 1338.2% year over year. Obligations by fiscal year rose from $0 in FY21 and $0 in FY22 to $259M in FY23, $121M in FY24, $928M in FY25, and $13.4B in FY26. Current-year totals are partial because the period is fiscal year to date. These figures are contract obligations except for award-value figures in other tables, which are total contract values. The FY26 total represents the largest single-year obligation to date for Fisher Sand and Gravel. Procurement and contracting professionals assessing federal participation should note the concentration of obligations in FY26 and the presence of large awards implied by the $890M average award size and the 15 awards recorded so far.",
